<title>USA: Simula restates 1995 results lower.</title>
<headline>Simula restates 1995 results lower.</headline>
<dateline>PHOENIX 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Simula Inc Tuesday said it restated 1995 net income lower by $1.45 million and earnings per share lower by $0.17 to record $2.4 million of estimated losses on two contracts acquired in connection with the 1994 acquisition of Artcraft Industries Corp.</p>
<p>Simula said it made the adjustment after discussions with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>Simula said its restated 1995 net income was $2,657,359 or $0.31 per share.</p>
<p>Simula said it had previously evaluated the losses as a pre-acquisition contingency and recorded them as goodwill.</p>
<p>Simula said the 1995 financial statements have been restated to reflect the reclassification of the estimated losses from goodwill to cost of revenue.</p>
</text>
